# CI-only patterns — files/paths that NEVER trigger source pipelines.
#
# Shape is gitignore-style:
#   - one pattern per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored
#   - `foo/`               subtree prefix match  (matches foo/<anything>)
#   - `path/to/file`       exact path match      (anchored)
#   - `CLAUDE.md`          basename match anywhere in the tree
#
# This is the single source of truth. Consumed by:
#   - genesis/orchestrator/Jenkinsfile         (auto-mode change detection)
#   - genesis/orchestrator/ci-ignore.mjs       (shared JS parser/matcher + CLI filter)
#   - genesis/orchestrator/orchestrator-strategy.mjs  (preview + tests, via ci-ignore.mjs)
#   - genesis/orchestrator/graph-walker.mjs    (CLI pre-filter, via ci-ignore.mjs)
#   - .husky/pre-push                          (pipes $CHANGED through ci-ignore.mjs)
# All load this file at runtime — no mirroring, no drift. (Jenkinsfile
# is Groovy and reimplements the parser; drift is caught by tests.)
#
# Before adding a basename: verify NO project's build/storybook/test
# pipeline reads the file by name as a real source input.

# Orchestrator + IDE/agent glue (entire subtrees):
.claude/
.github/
.husky/

# Specific CI-only files (orchestrator self-hosting + meta-doc):
ROADMAP.md
genesis/orchestrator/Jenkinsfile
genesis/orchestrator/build-graph.groovy

# Agent-instruction files anywhere in the tree.
# These live INSIDE product trees as developer guidance for AI coding
# agents, but are never consumed by any build/test/storybook step.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.no-claude.md
